From 9d572b9e94dcbc3736842c69d71b6c21d47638b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bmsohwinc <bharasou58@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 02:26:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] smf: use UPF-allocated N3 endpoints for the single-tunnel
 experiment

SMF currently sends its own uplink TEID and the shared configured N3 address to the gNB. That prevents one UPF-C from returning different worker endpoints for different sessions.

Record the FTUP capability during PFCP association and request IPv4 N3 allocation with CH=1. Consume Created PDR in establishPfcpSession before reporting success, match the returned PDR ID to the pending session request, and reject missing or invalid allocations. Store the resolved F-TEID in the existing PDR and update its uplink tunnel TEID.

Build the N2 setup message from the resolved session endpoint. Suppress the additional NR-DC tunnel advertisement in FTUP mode because the experiment allocates one tunnel per UE. Keep the configured endpoint behavior when FTUP is absent, leave the gNB's downlink TEID path intact, and retain LocalULTeid as SMF allocator bookkeeping rather than freeing a UPF-assigned ID through that allocator.

Based on 7ee22436f184000f25c3a348624559998eeb6e62. The experiment supports one IPv4 N3 allocation/PDR per session. Existing per-session QER management and PFCP dependencies are unchanged. Add focused tests for two distinct N2 endpoints, invalid allocations, response-buffer ownership, and legacy endpoint selection.
